{
  "id": "bigville_move_energy",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "description": "Per-agent ENERGY budget for bigville R1 (block 249000). `mv_energy_budget` is THE slow-down decision: the per-tick move budget is a graded step function of energy (3/2/1/0 hops as the budget nears threshold) \u2014 the agent SLOWS as it tires; thresholds are per-character (population variation). `mv_deplete` spends energy per applied hop, HUNGER-MODULATED (cost*(1+hunger)). Ablations are graph data: slow_on=0 -> flat budget; energy_cost=0 -> no depletion (both -> no slow-down, the load-bearing control). Composes existing Terms (IfThenElse/Gte/Max/Minus/Times/Plus) \u2014 zero new Rust.",
  "nodes": [],
  "edges": [],
  "productions": [],
  "concepts": [],
  "rules": [
